    "description": "Observe repeated Close and independent Open results after closing the sink's underlying file descriptor before its first Close. Add observable experiment-legality conditions while preserving the selected scope and oracle.",
    "claim_id": "O_snapshot_close_publication",
    "scope": {
      "description": "Sequential calls on one built-in FileSnapshotSink: successful creation and writes, an injected finalization failure before publication, observation of that error, and a second Close. Compare the second result with independent store availability immediately afterward.",
      "assumptions": [
        "The initial finalization failure occurs before directory publication.",
        "No concurrent writer, cancellation, external file deletion, snapshot replacement, or retention operation intervenes.",
        "The availability observation itself encounters no newly injected storage fault.",
        "The expectation interprets Close's documented successful end as a finalization result, including repeated calls; this applicability interpretation requires correspondence review."
      ],
      "excluded": [
        "Whether an application Persist implementation legally suppresses the first Close error",
        "Reachability of metadata advancement or log reclamation through takeSnapshot",
        "Crash durability and recovery after restart",
        "Failures occurring after directory publication",
        "Overall consensus safety or actual loss of recoverable history"
      ],
      "parameters": []
    },
